      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "1. Rearrange the original equation:  $2x + 3y - 6 = 0$, so  $3y = 6 - 2x$, and then  $y = - \\dfrac{2}{3} x + 2$, which implies  the slope of this line is  $- \\dfrac{2}{3}$.\n2. The slope of a line perpendicular to a given line is the negative reciprocal of the slope of the given line. Given the slope of the original equation is $- \\dfrac{2}{3}$, the slope of the line perpendicular to it is $ \\boxed{\\dfrac{3}{2}}$.",
